      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`test/registered/unit/kernels/test_jit_cache.py` fails on Intel XPU (BMG) with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tvm_ffi'` for every case that builds a ninja file, e.g. `test_build_key_separates_every_build_input[ldflags]`.\n\n`ninja.generate()` calls `toolchain.base_include_paths()` / `base_link_flags()`, which import `tvm_ffi` through `tvm_ffi_paths()`. `apache-tvm-ffi` is a core dependency in `pyproject.toml` but is not in `pyproject_xpu.toml`, so it is absent on XPU images.\n\n## Modifications\n\nTest-only change: an autouse fixture replaces `toolchain.tvm_ffi_paths` with fixed fake paths **only when `tvm_ffi` cannot be found**. These tests check build-key and ninja-text invariants, so only the paths' text matters.\n\nNo library code changes and no new dependency. CUDA/ROCm/MUSA/CPU lanes have `tvm_ffi` installed, so the stub never turns on there and their behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\nRan `test_jit_cache.py` on current main in a CPU venv:\n\n| Setup | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Without `tvm_ffi`, before this PR | 17 failed, 27 passed |\n| Without `tvm_ffi`, with this PR | 44 passed |\n| With `apache-tvm-ffi==0.1.11`, with this PR | 44 passed |\n\npre-commit passes on the changed file.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #41852057997](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41852057997)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41852057799](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41852057799)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #41852057987](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41852057987)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
